On 2007-08-04, Jove <invalid@invalid.invalid> wrote:
>   Skill slot management and weapons for Healers are a nightmare.  This

Given that the Healer has no skills to speak of worth advancing past 'Basic'
except for dagger and your final quarterstaff, I cannot imagine that 
"nightmare" is the correct word to use here.

Obtaining a decent weapon early on can be a pain in the ass.

> may be intentional.  The staff of Aesculapius is two-handed.  That
> means no shield (Up to +9 AC) and can be a deathtrap in Gehennom if
> cursed.  

Artifacts resist cursing, and more than -20 AC is unnecessary.

Fear is the mind-killer.  Keep holy water handy and rebless the Staff
anytime it becomes uncursed, and you'll never have a problem.

>   The staff also turns to junk from Gehennom on as more and more
> monsters are level-drain resistant.  

Only the following monsters are level-drain resistant:

all undead, all demons, all werefoo, and Death.

Undead and demons respect Elbereth, and as such it doesn't matter how 
long it takes you to kill them by beating them to death with a +7 staff.  
You can also just use Elbereth to go around them, as they'll start
running away and leave you space to move.

Werefoo are not worth mentioning, leaving Death the only problem.

Far more monsters in Gehennom are _not_ level-drain resistant, and the
Staff is a murderous death machine against those.  Wield it and win.

> Must be wielded for hungerless regeneration.  Must be #invoked for 
> healing.  The Wizard will try to steal it. 

The Wizard should never get more than a single turn against you in 
vanilla, and he will always attempt to steal the Amulet first.

> (I want to like the Staff.  I just can't.  Blame the
